WEBVTT

00:02.294 --> 00:04.589
<i>♪ it seems today
 that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.633 --> 00:07.637
<i>♪ is violence in movies
 and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:07.765 --> 00:11.354
<i>♪ but where are those
 good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.440 --> 00:14.360
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.446 --> 00:17.994
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.079 --> 00:21.334
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
 positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.420 --> 00:22.880
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:22.965 --> 00:24.132
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.259 --> 00:30.145
<i>♪ he's... A...
 Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:36.243 --> 00:37.870
What are you up to
there, stewie?

00:37.914 --> 00:41.336
Big birthday party today,
just finishing up my card.

00:41.422 --> 00:43.884
"happy birthday, gurt"?

00:44.011 --> 00:45.554
Yeah, it's short for "yogurt."

00:45.640 --> 00:48.185
His mom is a doula
and his dad is a doula.

00:48.312 --> 00:49.646
I like the blue truck.

00:49.774 --> 00:51.442
Thanks. It was supposed
to be a fire engine,

00:51.569 --> 00:53.446
But I couldn't find
the red glitter pen.

00:53.573 --> 00:56.202
Well, that's our long-form
tax return done.

00:56.329 --> 00:58.039
I could be wrong, but I think

00:58.167 --> 00:59.417
We're getting
a million dollars back.

00:59.503 --> 01:02.132
Oh, I'm glad you're here.
I ran out of bleach

01:02.217 --> 01:04.137
Halfway through
my mustache treatment today,

01:04.180 --> 01:06.099
So, peter, I'm gonna need you
to take stewie

01:06.184 --> 01:07.602
To the bowling alley
for a party.

01:07.729 --> 01:09.231
Hey, meg, I'm gonna need you
to take stewie

01:09.316 --> 01:10.943
To the bowling alley
for a party.

01:11.028 --> 01:12.697
I just learned the word
"delegate."

01:12.782 --> 01:15.452
No skin off my sack.
I love the bowling alley.

01:15.538 --> 01:16.706
I'm coming, too.

01:16.833 --> 01:19.211
They got a new claw machine
with a bra in it.

01:19.380 --> 01:22.594
We sure raised
a few fine delegates, huh?

01:22.679 --> 01:24.598
Peter, I don't think you
learned the word "delegate."

01:24.683 --> 01:27.730
I will not be delegated
in my own house.

01:27.815 --> 01:29.483
This is gonna be fun, stewie.

01:29.611 --> 01:31.654
Yeah, I'm pumped.
Partying's in our blood.

01:31.741 --> 01:34.661
We even had ancestors
at the boston tea party.

01:34.747 --> 01:36.373
All right,
let's stick it to the british

01:36.417 --> 01:38.044
And throw this tea overboard.

01:38.129 --> 01:39.547
How about this earl grey?

01:39.633 --> 01:41.176
Okay, you know what,
let's keep the earl grey.

01:41.261 --> 01:43.430
We-we all have to have
breakfast, right?

01:43.474 --> 01:45.936
-Here goes the chamomile.
-No, no, no. You throw that out,

01:46.064 --> 01:47.606
You're throwing
my good night's sleep away.

01:47.776 --> 01:49.861
How about this throat coat
with echinacea?

01:49.988 --> 01:51.657
Okay, you guys
are gonna hate me,

01:51.742 --> 01:53.035
But we're coming up
on cold and flu season.

01:53.120 --> 01:54.747
And I just think
that would be irresponsible.

01:54.874 --> 01:57.044
-Well, what about--
-you know what,
let's just boil some water

01:57.171 --> 01:59.549
And write 'em
a strongly-worded letter.

02:04.186 --> 02:05.521
Here you go, meg.

02:05.606 --> 02:08.151
You's all in lane six
with gurt's mother.

02:08.279 --> 02:10.197
Everybody wins.
Everybody wins here today.

02:10.283 --> 02:12.369
Gurt, get your hand
out of your pants!

02:12.454 --> 02:13.579
Thanks, bruce.

02:13.665 --> 02:15.543
Hey, want to put
quesadillas in our mouths

02:15.670 --> 02:17.338
<i>And flip through
a people magazine later?</i>

02:17.465 --> 02:19.969
Oh, I'd love to,
but this is our busiest day.

02:20.138 --> 02:22.391
I got five parties
and that guy over there

02:22.518 --> 02:25.481
Insists he can only bowl
like fred flintstone.

02:25.567 --> 02:28.112
Dad, you were coming here
the whole time?

02:28.197 --> 02:30.826
I don't have to tell you things
I'm keeping secret from you.

02:30.911 --> 02:32.078
All right, bruce, I'm up.

02:32.164 --> 02:34.083
[sighs]

02:34.169 --> 02:36.797
[xylophone playing]

02:42.520 --> 02:45.191
Yibba yabba yoo!

02:47.113 --> 02:48.991
[indistinct chatter]

02:49.118 --> 02:51.538
Stewie, william, you're up.

02:51.665 --> 02:55.213
Well, well, well, looks like
the new kid got a pity invite.

02:55.340 --> 02:56.465
My name's william.

02:56.509 --> 02:58.845
I've been on six airplanes.

02:59.014 --> 03:00.391
You do sports, william?

03:00.509 --> 03:02.521
You ever get your ass handed
to you, sports-wise?

03:02.606 --> 03:05.110
Not yet, stewie, but if
you throw the ball the way

03:05.195 --> 03:08.116
You threw back that cake,
you should be in good shape.

03:08.201 --> 03:10.162
Hope you got another set
of pins, bruce,

03:10.206 --> 03:12.291
'cause this one's
about to explode.

03:12.419 --> 03:14.129
Well, call me norma rae,

03:14.215 --> 03:16.175
'cause you're about
to see a strike.

03:16.261 --> 03:18.389
I watch a lot of movies
at my grandma's house.

03:20.270 --> 03:22.480
-On three?
-Oops.

03:23.276 --> 03:25.696
["the final countdown" by europe
playing]

03:57.936 --> 04:00.523
Yes! And then there were nine.

04:00.650 --> 04:01.775
It's not fair!

04:01.860 --> 04:04.405
Someone else was using
my lucky dinosaur ramp!

04:04.533 --> 04:07.036
Can't beat
the old strike-a-saurus!

04:07.122 --> 04:09.083
<i>♪ open the door,
 get on the floor ♪</i>

04:09.210 --> 04:12.382
<i>♪ everybody bowl
 that dinosaur. ♪</i>

04:16.267 --> 04:17.643
Are you here for shoes?

04:17.770 --> 04:19.605
Yeah, but I'm not sure
what size I am.

04:19.692 --> 04:22.152
The sizing line's
right over there.

04:22.281 --> 04:24.283
Just put your bare foot
on my stomach

04:24.410 --> 04:27.080
And I can tell you
your shoe size.

04:27.165 --> 04:29.043
I don't know. Next.

04:29.170 --> 04:30.462
Little higher.

04:30.548 --> 04:32.467
I don't know. Next.

04:33.388 --> 04:35.140
That'll do, pig.

04:35.183 --> 04:36.893
That'll do.

04:39.443 --> 04:40.568
Peter, you're up.

04:40.696 --> 04:43.491
Just got to dry my hands first.

04:43.619 --> 04:45.245
Ooh, how embarrassing.

04:45.331 --> 04:48.252
What an unexpected,
sexy turn of events.

04:48.379 --> 04:49.713
So, did you guys know that

04:49.757 --> 04:51.760
Marilyn's real name
was norma jean?

04:51.845 --> 04:54.140
-[sighs]
-mm-hmm.
-And if you said hello

04:54.309 --> 04:56.269
To bernard schwartz,
you'd be saying--

04:56.396 --> 04:58.358
Saying hello to tony curtis.
Yes, we know.

04:58.485 --> 05:01.155
"better smile
when you say that, pilgrim."

05:01.240 --> 05:04.537
Marion morrison, aka john wayne.

05:04.623 --> 05:07.335
Yep, we remember from the list
you emailed us, joe.

05:07.420 --> 05:09.840
You know, kennedy's secretary
was named lincoln,

05:09.926 --> 05:12.346
And lincoln's secretary
was named kennedy.

05:12.431 --> 05:14.601
-Kind of makes you think, huh?
-About what?

05:16.900 --> 05:18.944
Secretaries.

05:22.955 --> 05:24.790
Sorry we left such a mess.

05:24.875 --> 05:26.920
-Let me help you with that.
-Thanks, meg.

05:27.005 --> 05:28.924
Oop, looks like more vomit,

05:29.051 --> 05:31.138
And I done run out
of kitty litter to soak it up.

05:31.223 --> 05:34.185
That's all right, I always
keep a small bag in my purse.

05:34.312 --> 05:36.524
You keep kitty litter
in your purse?

05:36.609 --> 05:39.155
Well, there's not always
a bathroom when I need one.

05:39.282 --> 05:42.662
I don't know how you handle
all these kids every week.

05:42.748 --> 05:44.792
Oh, I don't mind.
I like children.

05:44.878 --> 05:46.421
Always wanted one of my own.

05:46.506 --> 05:48.216
Someone I could raise
a little bit better

05:48.302 --> 05:49.595
Than my parents did me.

05:49.680 --> 05:51.599
You'd be a great dad, bruce.

05:51.684 --> 05:53.644
You should totally have a kid.

05:53.731 --> 05:55.566
I don't know if you knew this,
but it's

05:55.693 --> 05:58.363
Anatomically impossible
for a man to get pregnant.

05:58.449 --> 05:59.909
Even lindsey graham?

05:59.994 --> 06:02.831
Well, he's certainly giving it
the ol' college try.

06:02.959 --> 06:05.003
But I guess it's just
not in the cards

06:05.047 --> 06:06.255
For jeffrey and me.

06:06.383 --> 06:08.887
After all, you can't make
a bun without a oven.

06:09.014 --> 06:11.183
Well, I have an oven.

06:11.268 --> 06:12.895
I mean, it may not
close all the way,

06:12.980 --> 06:16.236
And it's definitely not
self-cleaning, but it works.

06:16.363 --> 06:18.533
You should thank
your lucky stars for that.

06:18.618 --> 06:20.286
Well, I don't know
if you've noticed,

06:20.413 --> 06:22.542
But I don't exactly
have a lot of suitors.

06:22.627 --> 06:24.504
It might be
because you's going potty

06:24.631 --> 06:26.091
In your purse all the time.

06:26.176 --> 06:28.721
But at least
you's able to have a baby.

06:29.517 --> 06:30.475
You're right.

06:30.561 --> 06:32.564
I can have a baby.

06:33.359 --> 06:34.944
Mom, dad.

06:35.029 --> 06:37.073
I'm having
bruce and jeffrey's baby.

06:37.200 --> 06:38.743
That's wonderful.

06:38.912 --> 06:41.207
What do you say we take this
party to the top of the stairs?

06:42.378 --> 06:45.174
<i>[announcer] it's not an
 abortion, it's an "oopsie."</i>

06:50.939 --> 06:52.900
Meg, there is no way
you are having

06:52.985 --> 06:55.822
Bruce and jeffrey's baby.
I forbid it.

06:55.950 --> 06:58.579
We agreed no more kids in the
house unless it's young sheldon.

06:58.664 --> 07:00.791
Boy, is that kid a pepper pot.

07:00.877 --> 07:02.420
It's not what you guys think.

07:02.505 --> 07:03.673
I'm gonna be a surrogate.

07:03.800 --> 07:05.427
But don't you need an egg?

07:05.512 --> 07:07.598
Or-or is that...
Is that a bad question to ask

07:07.684 --> 07:09.603
Now that penises and vaginas
mean nothing?

07:09.730 --> 07:11.774
Jeffrey and bruce
already picked out

07:11.860 --> 07:13.361
An egg donor from a website.

07:13.446 --> 07:14.697
Okay, as your father,

07:14.866 --> 07:16.368
I'd like to say something.

07:16.453 --> 07:18.581
You can just get
hot eggs off the internet?

07:18.750 --> 07:21.044
Wh-what, uh, what, uh,
what, uh, wh-wha-- uh,

07:21.130 --> 07:23.926
Wh-wha-what website?

07:24.011 --> 07:25.888
[sighs]
meg, this is serious.

07:25.974 --> 07:28.227
Pregnancy is not something
you do for money

07:28.312 --> 07:30.315
Or to keep a certain
professional athlete interested

07:30.401 --> 07:32.027
After he blocks your number.

07:32.113 --> 07:34.658
You're gonna ruin your life,
and I won't have any part of it.

07:34.785 --> 07:37.831
Well, too bad, 'cause I'm 18
and you can't stop me.

07:37.917 --> 07:41.171
Dang, no more sush for meg
for nine whole months.

07:41.258 --> 07:43.635
That's honestly what you're
taking away from all this?

07:43.679 --> 07:45.724
Well, yeah.
I'm still getting sush.

07:45.809 --> 07:48.104
Anyone else for sush? Dad, sush?

07:48.231 --> 07:50.233
Ma, sush? Chris, sush?

07:50.318 --> 07:51.945
Meg, no sush.
Don't even answer, meg.

07:52.031 --> 07:53.867
She's like,
"aw, I want sush so bad."

07:53.952 --> 07:56.581
I'm like,
"no, no, meg, no sush, babe."

07:56.666 --> 07:58.251
Anyway, I'm gonna go out
and get some sush.

07:58.336 --> 08:00.840
I'll be at cvs.

08:05.018 --> 08:07.145
Aw, this is embarrassing.
We wore the same thing.

08:07.273 --> 08:10.820
Let it be noted that I was
the one to change this time.

08:10.906 --> 08:12.866
Anyway, good news.
The fertilization

08:12.951 --> 08:15.664
Of the hella-more-attractive egg
was a success.

08:15.750 --> 08:17.292
Brucie, we did it.

08:17.420 --> 08:19.547
I'm gonna dress him
in political t-shirts

08:19.633 --> 08:21.761
He can't even begin
to understand.

08:21.846 --> 08:23.556
Yes, so now we just
have to implant

08:23.683 --> 08:26.312
That very hot embryo
into meg's body.

08:26.397 --> 08:27.899
-Is this gonna hurt?
-Not at all.

08:28.068 --> 08:30.530
Nurse, wheel
in the implantation cannon.

08:30.657 --> 08:32.075
You guys are gonna
love this thing.

08:32.160 --> 08:35.332
A clown died in there,
but I think we got him all out.

08:54.626 --> 08:57.046
Can someone please go get me
a cup of buffalo sauce

08:57.132 --> 08:59.302
And a hollowed-out pickle
to use as a straw

08:59.387 --> 09:00.929
To suck up the sauce?

09:01.016 --> 09:03.561
Fine, but I'm making you
a grilled cheese.

09:03.646 --> 09:05.481
And not because
I support this pregnancy.

09:05.525 --> 09:08.404
I just enjoy making passive-
aggressive grilled cheeses

09:08.489 --> 09:09.699
For people
and then saying, "here,

09:09.784 --> 09:12.413
Here's your freakin'
grilled cheese."

09:12.498 --> 09:14.710
[sniffing]
hey, meg?

09:14.837 --> 09:16.589
How many farts
you been blasting off today?

09:16.716 --> 09:18.636
We talking bigs and smalls?

09:18.721 --> 09:20.473
Fronts? Backs? Wets? Drys?

09:20.558 --> 09:23.020
Ah. Well, I am gonna run
out of this room now

09:23.105 --> 09:26.026
And leave a comedically-
shaped hole in the wall.

09:26.905 --> 09:27.989
That was already there

09:28.075 --> 09:29.868
From dad's
drunk driving accident.

09:29.954 --> 09:31.956
[peter]
nope! Running from farts!

09:35.883 --> 09:38.428
Man, meg being pregnant
is almost as bad

09:38.555 --> 09:40.057
As when that other lady
was pregnant.

09:40.184 --> 09:42.771
'member? The lady
with the loose baked-eggs rack?

09:42.898 --> 09:44.901
-'member her?
-Peter, that was me.

09:44.987 --> 09:46.822
And no way
was I worse than this.

09:46.949 --> 09:48.868
Well, maybe this'll turn out
better than you think,

09:48.954 --> 09:52.334
Like eating edible underwear
in non-sexual situations.

09:52.420 --> 09:56.092
I can't believe you chose this
for your last meal.

09:56.219 --> 09:58.639
Well, I guess
we're both "shocked" today.

09:58.725 --> 10:01.813
Okay, fellas, light me up.

10:01.982 --> 10:04.110
You know what, he's funny.

10:04.195 --> 10:06.156
Now I see why our daughter
got in that van.

10:06.283 --> 10:09.330
-[crackling]
-[peter] yibba yabba yoo!

10:09.415 --> 10:10.958
Well, maybe you're right.

10:11.085 --> 10:13.046
I'm just glad
this day's finally over.

10:13.131 --> 10:15.217
-Night, peter.
-Night, lois.

10:16.388 --> 10:18.641
[meg]
mom! Dad!

10:18.727 --> 10:20.228
[groans]
just ignore her.

10:20.356 --> 10:21.899
She'll tire herself out.

10:21.984 --> 10:23.652
[meg]
dad! Mom!

10:23.738 --> 10:24.989
Please!

10:25.075 --> 10:26.993
Lois. The daughter's crying.

10:27.079 --> 10:28.955
[meg]
I'm super wide awake

10:29.041 --> 10:30.960
And I want to eat something
really rank.

10:31.046 --> 10:32.589
Lois, did you hear that?

10:32.674 --> 10:34.593
[lois snoring]

10:34.637 --> 10:35.762
[sighs]

10:35.847 --> 10:38.017
Okay. I guess I got this one.

10:43.824 --> 10:46.119
Papa john,
I'm sorry to bother you,

10:46.204 --> 10:48.123
But my pregnant daughter
asked that I bring her

10:48.166 --> 10:50.670
The worst pizza ever,
and yours is that.

10:50.797 --> 10:52.925
You think we're worse
than lunchables?

10:53.010 --> 10:54.261
-Yes.
-7-eleven?

10:54.389 --> 10:56.141
Look, my friend,
my friend, my friend.

10:56.268 --> 10:58.520
It's late,
we've done our research.

10:58.648 --> 11:00.149
The sauce,
the bread, the toppings,

11:00.277 --> 11:02.195
The way it's cooked,
the people cooking it,

11:02.322 --> 11:04.492
The way it tastes
like the box it comes in.

11:04.619 --> 11:06.413
It's really, really the worst.

11:06.498 --> 11:08.993
I mean, you even make
butter dipping sauce terrible.

11:09.045 --> 11:11.716
Well, do you want the butter
sauce with the pizza or not?

11:11.843 --> 11:14.180
Yeah, no, give me
a bunch of everything.

11:18.775 --> 11:20.694
[sighs]
what do you want, chris?

11:20.779 --> 11:22.991
-Is it pump time yet?
-Why do you care?

11:23.076 --> 11:26.373
Meg, I'm a member of a very
specific dark web internet site.

11:26.459 --> 11:27.709
Don't try to find it,
you won't be able to.

11:27.878 --> 11:30.591
But this would be
fairly monumental there.

11:30.718 --> 11:32.762
Mom, chris is being disgusting.

11:32.847 --> 11:34.725
So are you.
We're all disgusting.

11:34.810 --> 11:36.938
-That's what family is.
-[groans]

11:37.023 --> 11:38.943
I knew this was a bad idea.

11:39.028 --> 11:40.445
Yeah, marriage blows.

11:40.532 --> 11:42.325
No, I mean meg's pregnancy.

11:42.452 --> 11:44.120
I wish we could
just fast-forward through

11:44.206 --> 11:45.958
The next couple of months
until she gives birth

11:46.085 --> 11:48.255
And this whole thing blows over.

11:51.054 --> 11:54.351
Well, team, I tried meth.

11:56.483 --> 11:59.279
All right, guys, looks
like I'm really liking meth.

12:01.326 --> 12:03.204
Hey, guys, I need money.

12:03.331 --> 12:05.458
Like, now.
Like, yesterday! Like, now!

12:08.509 --> 12:10.219
Hi, peter, my name is marcus.

12:10.263 --> 12:11.973
Your family has written
some letters

12:12.100 --> 12:13.476
They'd like to read to you.

12:13.562 --> 12:15.480
You liars!

12:21.078 --> 12:23.205
Weird easter this year.

12:25.504 --> 12:26.964
Dad, you're back!

12:27.050 --> 12:28.885
Ah, we missed you so much.

12:28.970 --> 12:30.388
Ah, I missed you guys.

12:30.515 --> 12:32.476
Meth was great,
but I guess it's bad.

12:32.561 --> 12:34.397
I don't know, I'm not
really sold on that yet.

12:34.483 --> 12:35.941
We're proud of you, peter.

12:36.028 --> 12:39.232
Uh, guys?
I think my water just broke.

12:39.284 --> 12:41.412
Oh, right,
I forgot we were doing that.

12:43.795 --> 12:45.380
[panting]

12:45.507 --> 12:48.219
Well, I see nobody
brought me a doctor gift.

12:48.346 --> 12:50.265
That's fine,
you still have a year.

12:50.309 --> 12:52.728
Meg, I'm just going
to check the contractions.

12:52.815 --> 12:54.525
"should've, would've, hadn't,

12:54.694 --> 12:57.739
Ma'am, 'twas." oh, they're
getting closer together.

12:57.826 --> 13:00.286
It's coming! It's coming!

13:00.415 --> 13:02.500
Okay, we're out of gloves,
so I'm gonna catch it

13:02.627 --> 13:04.212
With this panda express bag.

13:04.297 --> 13:05.757
Are you sure this
is safe?

13:05.884 --> 13:07.469
Oh, yeah,
panda bags are medical-grade.

13:07.596 --> 13:09.014
Just never use a subway bag.

13:09.100 --> 13:10.852
I've had, like, four
go right through.

13:10.979 --> 13:12.856
Uhp, it's in the bag already.

13:12.942 --> 13:14.359
It's a girl.

13:14.445 --> 13:16.281
What's that big
ol' vine coming out?

13:16.366 --> 13:19.245
<i>She looks like one of them
pumpkins in cinderella.</i>

13:20.459 --> 13:22.627
♪ ♪

13:23.673 --> 13:25.593
She...

13:25.636 --> 13:27.472
She's beautiful.

13:27.557 --> 13:29.559
[crying]

13:30.731 --> 13:32.557
Ooh, that's awful loud.

13:32.610 --> 13:35.405
Yeah, that's a pee-poo-mix
cry if I ever heard one.

13:35.491 --> 13:37.911
And it'll be a weird poo,
that first one, trust me.

13:38.038 --> 13:39.748
You-you know
that volcano in hawaii

13:39.834 --> 13:42.588
Where the lava just slowly rolls
through people's yards?

13:42.673 --> 13:44.175
It's like that, only poo.

13:44.260 --> 13:47.306
That does sound like
a lot to deal with.

13:47.434 --> 13:50.605
So, do you clean that up with,
like, kleenex and febreezes?

13:50.691 --> 13:53.654
You know what, why don't
I take the first shift?

13:53.781 --> 13:56.786
Well, it would give us a chance
to finish doo-dadding her room.

13:56.830 --> 13:58.331
And we have to buy every product

13:58.458 --> 14:01.245
Of known baby expert
jessica alba.

14:01.297 --> 14:03.676
Well, sounds like you guys
have a lot to talk about.

14:03.803 --> 14:06.098
Thanks, meg.
We'll text you tomorrow.

14:06.267 --> 14:09.438
Welcome to the world,
little liza judy barbra.

14:11.278 --> 14:13.364
All right, sush time for meg.

14:13.449 --> 14:15.535
I know you want
some hospital sush.

14:15.620 --> 14:18.124
No? Dad? Sush? Pepsi max?

14:18.209 --> 14:20.170
Ma? Diet max? Sush?

14:20.256 --> 14:22.843
Chris? Max? Code red? Sush?

14:22.928 --> 14:25.599
No? Well, I'm getting
some sush and a max.

14:25.726 --> 14:27.394
I'll be at the cafeteria.

14:28.691 --> 14:30.359
Don't get the sush, guys.

14:36.333 --> 14:38.335
[crying]

14:41.051 --> 14:43.262
Okay, okay, liza judy barbra.

14:43.348 --> 14:46.686
It's time for the bottle because
I forgot to tweeze my nips.

14:46.772 --> 14:48.398
[crying]

14:48.517 --> 14:51.489
This is getting ridiculous.
It's been three days.

14:51.574 --> 14:54.370
Why haven't bruce and jeffrey
picked up their baby?

14:54.455 --> 14:57.293
I don't know.
They're, like, super busy.

14:57.379 --> 14:58.922
Hey, look at the bright side,
lois.

14:59.049 --> 15:00.174
With that baby around,
you look like

15:00.259 --> 15:01.719
The hottest grandma in town.

15:01.846 --> 15:03.808
[scoffs]
the hottest grandma?

15:03.935 --> 15:05.937
The-the hottest grandma?
[chuckles]

15:06.064 --> 15:08.609
[cackles]

15:08.778 --> 15:10.614
The hottest grandma!

15:10.783 --> 15:13.787
Ha-ha! Well, I mean, okay.

15:13.915 --> 15:16.001
The hottest grandma
should be jennifer aniston,

15:16.128 --> 15:18.589
But the counting crows guy
wasn't ready to commit.

15:18.717 --> 15:21.847
Poor bastard thought
it was gonna be an endless run.

15:25.273 --> 15:26.983
That was bruce and jeffrey.

15:27.068 --> 15:30.407
They're not coming to get liza
judy barbra until tomorrow now.

15:30.534 --> 15:31.994
Ugh. Why not?

15:32.121 --> 15:34.332
Not that you guys care
about this sort of thing,

15:34.418 --> 15:36.378
But jeffrey wrote
a murder mystery that premieres

15:36.464 --> 15:39.218
Tonight at the cracker barrel
in sturbridge.

15:40.056 --> 15:41.222
Oh, no!

15:41.308 --> 15:43.644
Yeah, but
if you's got to go...

15:43.772 --> 15:45.816
[dramatic sting plays]

15:49.743 --> 15:53.123
I made this a cutaway
so I could see the show.

15:55.631 --> 15:57.509
Peekaboo!

15:57.636 --> 15:58.886
[speaking gibberish]

15:58.971 --> 16:00.389
[laughs]

16:00.475 --> 16:02.686
-[laughing]
-[farting]

16:07.825 --> 16:10.537
[chuckles] yeah, yeah, it's
hard to laugh without farting.

16:10.572 --> 16:13.292
Feels like you and me are on the
same page about a lot of stuff.

16:13.419 --> 16:16.843
We work well together,
like the employees at t.J. Maxx.

16:16.970 --> 16:18.470
Hey, where should I put these?

16:18.557 --> 16:20.475
Just throw them on the floor
and step on them.

16:20.561 --> 16:22.730
That's our founder's motto.

16:23.734 --> 16:25.987
<i>[announcer] t.J. Maxx.
 Teach your kids to drive</i>

16:26.073 --> 16:27.867
<i> In our empty parking lot.</i>

16:32.880 --> 16:34.506
Guys, look.

16:34.592 --> 16:37.262
Look at me.
Now that I'm a hot grandma,

16:37.347 --> 16:39.475
I bought one of those
novelty wine glasses

16:39.561 --> 16:42.106
That's big enough to hold
an entire bottle of wine.

16:42.192 --> 16:44.485
Isn't that hilarious?

16:45.991 --> 16:47.911
It's okay.

16:47.996 --> 16:49.371
That was worth it for the joke.

16:49.457 --> 16:50.750
You did good, lois.

16:50.835 --> 16:52.462
You're building a comedic voice.

16:52.547 --> 16:56.220
Okay. Here we go,
liza judy barbra.

16:56.348 --> 16:59.268
Your first strained peas.

17:01.233 --> 17:03.527
Wow, she is the most memorable

17:03.613 --> 17:06.242
And endearing baby
I've ever seen.

17:06.327 --> 17:08.455
Okay, then.

17:08.540 --> 17:10.292
[grunting]

17:10.419 --> 17:12.881
Oh, I'm sorry, are you...
Are you almost done?

17:12.967 --> 17:15.136
Oh, yeah, no, sorry,
I'm just, I'm doing sets.

17:15.222 --> 17:17.600
-I'm just doing little sets.
-Oh, cool, cool.

17:17.686 --> 17:19.437
-Guys, he's doing little sets.
-Cool, cool.

17:19.564 --> 17:21.024
-Little sets.
-Cool, cool.

17:21.110 --> 17:22.820
Meg, I am so impressed.

17:22.905 --> 17:25.367
Yeah, I had no idea
you could be so maternal.

17:25.494 --> 17:27.831
I always saw you as
a "drive into the lake" mom.

17:27.916 --> 17:29.334
So did I, mom.

17:29.503 --> 17:32.340
But, honestly,
since liza judy barbra was born,

17:32.468 --> 17:36.016
I feel like my life has
purpose for the first time.

17:36.143 --> 17:37.477
[singsongy] knock-knock.

17:37.563 --> 17:39.273
I know this may be
not a good time,

17:39.358 --> 17:41.402
But we just had
to come see our little angel.

17:41.487 --> 17:43.072
"had to come see"?

17:43.158 --> 17:44.409
Where have you two been?

17:44.494 --> 17:46.538
<i>Watching mamma mia
and making popovers.</i>

17:46.623 --> 17:48.335
What is wrong with you two?

17:48.462 --> 17:50.255
How irresponsible can you be?

17:50.299 --> 17:52.384
I mean, this is your daughter
you abandoned.

17:52.470 --> 17:54.639
Abandoned?
We wanted to come over,

17:54.725 --> 17:56.978
But meg kept saying
it was a bad time.

17:57.064 --> 17:59.525
Meg, is that true?

18:03.285 --> 18:06.457
[sighs]
this baby needs me.

18:06.626 --> 18:09.171
It's the first living thing
that's ever needed me.

18:09.256 --> 18:11.844
For once, my life has purpose.

18:11.888 --> 18:13.263
And I'm good at this.

18:13.391 --> 18:15.101
Better than these two, anyway.

18:15.229 --> 18:16.604
Maybe she's right.

18:16.731 --> 18:19.151
What businesses
do we have raising a child?

18:19.278 --> 18:21.573
And how's is we supposed
to pay for her school?

18:21.659 --> 18:23.829
With our tesla
and cashmere money?

18:23.956 --> 18:25.248
I don't think so.

18:25.334 --> 18:27.838
We could dip into
our boozy brunch fund.

18:28.006 --> 18:29.132
Don't you dare.

18:29.259 --> 18:30.718
Oh, listen to me.

18:30.804 --> 18:33.391
I wouldn't know
how to raise a baby.

18:33.518 --> 18:36.565
I'm sure she knows that, too.

18:36.692 --> 18:38.694
♪ ♪

18:40.116 --> 18:41.242
Gaga.

18:41.369 --> 18:42.870
[gasps] gaga?

18:42.998 --> 18:44.248
Bruce, did you hear that?

18:44.333 --> 18:46.837
She said her first gay icon.

18:46.922 --> 18:48.007
Jeanne tripplehorn.

18:48.092 --> 18:51.389
Oh, my god,
a second, lesser-known gay icon.

18:51.475 --> 18:53.143
She wants her daddies.

18:53.228 --> 18:54.604
Meg, I'm sorry.

18:54.647 --> 18:57.444
I know we're not perfect,
but no parent is.

18:57.529 --> 18:59.114
And this is our child.

18:59.241 --> 19:00.492
She belongs with us.

19:00.620 --> 19:03.165
But you don't know anything
about raising a child.

19:03.209 --> 19:04.501
No one does.

19:04.586 --> 19:07.299
That's why two out of three
don't turn out right.

19:07.426 --> 19:09.553
But that doesn't mean
you don't try.

19:09.639 --> 19:11.642
♪ ♪

19:14.691 --> 19:17.988
Meg, we'll always appreciate
what you've done for us.

19:18.115 --> 19:21.412
And you'll always be a part
of liza judy barbra's life.

19:21.582 --> 19:24.836
Yeah. You'll always be
that slightly creepy teen

19:24.965 --> 19:28.303
Who birthed our baby and then
we gradually lost touch with.

19:28.472 --> 19:30.140
You better promise.

19:30.226 --> 19:31.769
-We do.
-We do.

19:31.896 --> 19:33.648
In that case...

19:35.445 --> 19:38.116
...I'll take a chance on you.

19:38.243 --> 19:39.911
<i>[off-key]
♪ if you're all alone ♪</i>

19:39.997 --> 19:42.125
<i>♪ when the pretty birds
 have flown... ♪</i>

19:42.210 --> 19:45.591
-No!
-That can't be the first time
our baby hears abba.

19:45.676 --> 19:48.514
That's right. It should be
at a jockstrap foam rave

19:48.600 --> 19:50.226
In miami beach, same as me.

19:50.353 --> 19:51.980
What? Wait!

19:52.065 --> 19:53.734
But-but I'm the hot grandma!

19:53.819 --> 19:56.114
[gasps]
you're a grandma?

19:56.199 --> 19:58.243
You look amazing!

19:58.287 --> 20:00.373
Oh, you. Come on.

20:00.459 --> 20:02.669
Could a grandma wear this
to a spin class?

20:02.797 --> 20:05.468
I mean, yes, she could,
because I did,

20:05.595 --> 20:07.347
So that happened.

20:07.432 --> 20:08.382
Thank you, meg.

20:08.517 --> 20:10.061
You've completed our family.

20:10.146 --> 20:13.401
We have our baby
and we have you.

20:13.528 --> 20:14.738
Well, I guess that means

20:14.823 --> 20:17.243
I can get rid
of all my hot grandma merch.

20:17.371 --> 20:19.414
I'll just donate it to goodwill.

20:19.542 --> 20:21.586
You know what "gilf" means,
right?

20:21.672 --> 20:24.092
Yeah. "god, I love fentanyl."

20:24.260 --> 20:25.804
You said it, pal.

20:31.568 --> 20:33.487
Well, bruce and jeffrey,
I got to say,

20:33.572 --> 20:35.116
You two have really stepped up

20:35.201 --> 20:37.162
To become
a couple of great dads.

20:37.289 --> 20:38.248
Thank you, lois.

20:38.291 --> 20:39.542
You sound a bit surprised,

20:39.627 --> 20:42.047
Which seems right
for a woman with that haircut,

20:42.133 --> 20:44.511
But you're sweet to say so.

20:44.596 --> 20:46.265
-[fussing]
-uh-oh.

20:46.393 --> 20:48.603
Someone's being
a little fussy britches.

20:48.689 --> 20:49.898
Oh, she's tired.

20:49.984 --> 20:52.279
You get the lights
and I'll sing her to sleep.

20:52.364 --> 20:53.823
[fussing continues]

20:53.951 --> 20:56.455
[imitating thumping
club bass beat]

20:56.540 --> 20:58.960
[fussing stops]

20:59.087 --> 21:01.799
Yeah, that seems about right
for a guy with that haircut.

21:01.885 --> 21:04.013
[quietly] thank you, peter.